What each component does:
Component	Purpose
EC2	Hosts the complete solution
Ollama	Downloads, manages and runs LLMs
Llama	The actual language model
Open WebUI	Provides the ChatGPT-like interface
EBS	Stores downloaded model files and application data

The important distinction: Ollama is not the LLM. It is the runtime that runs the LLM. Open WebUI is the frontend.
2. EC2 instance sizing
The instance selection depends on which Llama model you want to run.
Model	Approx. model download	Suggested starting configuration
Llama 3.2 1B	1.3 GB	2 vCPU, 8 GB RAM
Llama 3.2 3B	2 GB	2–4 vCPU, 8–16 GB RAM
Llama 3.1 8B	4.9 GB	4 vCPU, 16 GB RAM; GPU preferred
Llama 3.3 70B	40+ GB	Multi-GPU/high-memory configuration

These are approximate quantized model sizes; actual memory requirements also depend on context length and concurrent users. 
